      "writtenOn": "2022-12-19T08:48:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought it’s better to make the script fail if the desc.json contains unsupported/unexpected arch difference instead of silently ignore.\nSo that we can realize the issue early and fix the script or fix the upstream.\n\nTarget can have different values for input/output technically.\nI do agree that currently we don’t want to support actions which will be converted to the module which have different values for some attributes (e.g. tool_files, outputs)\n`merge_modules` fails in above cases. (aosp/2361731) so we can be always sure desc.json desn’t contain unexpected arch difference.\n \nThis validation can be done in gn_utils but I think gn_utils doesn\u0027t need to reject this case as far as it’s a valid gn target and gn_utils doesn\u0027t need to know much about our conversion logic from .gn to .bp.\nAlso, some sanitizer could change inputs/outputs, so I made `inputs/outputs/script` arch attributes and added validation at merge process in gen_android_bp.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCurrently, Target has the Arch specific attributes and common attributes and gn_utils optimize/finalize them before passing target to the gen_android_bp\n\nBut I’m feeling this makes the gen_android_bp complicated.\nFor example,\ngen_android_bp does similar dependency processing for target and arch.\nAlso gen_android_bp needs to dig into the arch even when it processing the target (e.g. `merge_attribute`)\n\nWhat I’m thinking is\ngn_utils will populate complete Target for each architecture, gen_android_bp convert each target to the module(s) after that gen_android_bp can merge modules if possible.\n\nMerging process would raise Error if there is unexpected/unsupported arch differences so that we are sure we are not ignoring unexpected arch differences.",
